     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single non-foothold step is a single point of failure. The target is an OR over dbReplica, vaultRead, shareMount and codeRepo, and every route has an alternative. tokenCache is reachable directly from footholds (wifiGuest, vpnGateway, exposedApi). It reaches appServer, then codeRepo, then the target, and appServer also reaches the target via shareMount. Separately, iotDevice (from exposedApi or wifiGuest) or containerHost (from internet, wifiGuest or supplychain) reaches memoryDump. memoryDump reaches monitoringHost, then shareMount, then the target, and also reaches appServer. Blocking appServer leaves memoryDump, monitoringHost, shareMount. Blocking memoryDump, monitoringHost or shareMount leaves tokenCache, appServer, codeRepo. Blocking tokenCache or codeRepo leaves the memoryDump route. iotDevice, containerHost, sshKey and every other step are bypassed by these two independent routes. So no single step blocks all paths.\"}"
    }
   ],
